From: brainux-pw-a9300
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: imx28-pwa7200: give the main LCD an enable gpio and its backlight

Of the three sharp,en GPIOs, only GPIO0_27 makes a visible difference
when low: the panel goes white, as if unpowered. GPIO0_26 and GPIO4_16
change nothing that can be seen. Move GPIO0_27 to enable-gpios, so the
driver lowers it while the display is off, and point the panel at its
backlight, so the backlight goes off with the display.

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/imx28-pwa7200.dts
@@ -46,8 +46,10 @@
 
 	sharp,en-gpios =
 	<&gpio0 26 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>,
-	<&gpio0 27 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>,
 	<&gpio4 16 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	/* Low turns the panel white, i.e. unpowered */
+	enable-gpios = <&gpio0 27 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	backlight = <&backlight_display>;
 };
 
 &slcd {
